course: dictionary
lesson: 13042
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «What a fantastic goal!» shows that fantastic means extremely good.
explain: In a story full of dragons, unicorns and magic lands, fantastic means strange and imaginary, not real. «The book was full of fantastic creatures.» The clues are the story and the word creatures.
explain: Fantastic can also mean very large. «She saved a fantastic amount of money.» Ask yourself what the sentence says about size. Then swap in very good or very big to see which one makes sense.
fact: Fantastic means extremely good, wonderful, as in «a fantastic party».
fact: Fantastic also means strange and imaginary, like something from a fantasy story, as in «fantastic creatures».
fact: A fantastic amount means a very large amount, as in «a fantastic sum of money».
fact: In everyday talk, people often say «fantastic!» to mean great, and this use is informal.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Your painting is fantastic, Ruby!» What does fantastic mean? | Strange and imaginary | Very sad | Very large | *Extremely good
exercise: «The book was full of fantastic creatures, like flying horses and talking trees.» What does fantastic suggest here? | Real animals found on a farm | *Strange and imaginary, from a fantasy story | Extremely good at maths | Very large in size
exercise: «The company made a fantastic amount of money this year.» What does fantastic mean here? | Very small | Dark | Slow | *Very large
test: «We had a fantastic time at the beach.» What does fantastic mean? | Very small | Cold and wet | Strange and imaginary | *Extremely good, wonderful
test: Finn says fantastic always means good. Is he right? | Yes, it only ever means good | Yes, it always means sad | *No, it can also mean strange and imaginary, or very large | No, it always means sleepy
exam: «The fantastic beasts in the film had scales and wings.» What does fantastic mean? | Extremely quiet | Very tired | *Strange and imaginary | Very hungry
